      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "Dawat-E-Islami USA demonstrates high spending efficiency by channeling a <cite id=\"1\">93.7% program expense ratio</cite> into its religious and educational activities [1]. In FY2025 tax filings, the charity managed <cite id=\"3\">$2,968,461 in revenue</cite> while keeping administrative and fundraising expenditures minimal [1][3]. Its financial health is further reinforced by holding <cite id=\"1\">20.2 months of working capital</cite>, providing significant stability [1]. Independent evaluation yields an <cite id=\"1\">overall score of 80.0/100 from Charity Navigator</cite>, highlighting solid leadership accountability [1]."
      ],
      "summary": "Dawat-E-Islami USA is a religious and educational non-profit that provides cultural programming, Quran Hifz, Nazra, and Aalim courses [3][4]. In FY2025 filings, the organization reported <cite id=\"3\">$2,968,461 in total revenue</cite>, reflecting steady general growth over recent years [3]. Operational spending is exceptionally lean, directing a <cite id=\"1\">93.7% program expense ratio</cite> straight to religious and educational activities [1]. This efficiency <cite id=\"1\">exceeds the 82.4% peer median</cite> for similar religious organizations [1]. Charity Navigator assigns the organization an <cite id=\"1\">overall score of 80/100</cite>, backed by strong leadership metrics [1]. While governance filings remain minimal, the organization exhibits robust operational health with significant working capital reserves [1][3]. Direct general contributions fund mosques, virtual learning via Faizan Online Academy, and educational literature distributions globally [3][6]. The organization operates under a SADAQAH-ELIGIBLE framework for donors supporting Islamic learning and community services [2].",
